{{!
    @template local_awareness/manage/cell_chips

    A list of chips, or a muted sentence when there are none.

    Used by the Behaviour column, which draws one chip per setting that is switched ON and nothing
    for the rest: an on/off pair told apart by colour is invisible to a reader with a colour vision
    deficiency, and absence carries "off" perfectly well while every chip present says what it is
    in words.

    Context variables required:
    * chips (array of {label}) — one entry per setting that is on
    * haschips (bool) — whether the list has anything in it
    * emptylabel (string) — the sentence shown when it does not

    Example context (json):
    {
        "haschips": true,
        "emptylabel": "Nothing set",
        "chips": [{"label": "Repeats every 1 day"}, {"label": "Requires acknowledgement"}]
    }
}}
{{#haschips}}
    <div class="local-awareness-chips">
        {{#chips}}<span class="local-awareness-chip">{{label}}</span>{{/chips}}
    </div>
{{/haschips}}
{{^haschips}}
    <span class="text-muted">{{emptylabel}}</span>
{{/haschips}}
